1
00:00:07,690 --> 00:00:11,850
A shop sells floor tiles priced for each square metre.

2
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:15,350
But your floor plan is in square centimetres.

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:19,020
The floor is 180,000 square centimetres.

4
00:00:19,070 --> 00:00:21,380
How many square metres is that?

5
00:00:21,430 --> 00:00:23,520
Be careful: it is not 1,800.

6
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:27,350
Pause the video and work it out.

7
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:29,950
1 metre is 100 centimetres.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,440
But 1 square metre is 100 centimetres by 100 centimetres.

9
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:39,260
That is 10,000 square centimetres.

10
00:00:39,310 --> 00:00:43,070
So divide by 10,000, not by 100.

11
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:49,090
180,000 divided by 10,000 is 18 square metres.

12
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:51,460
Remember the length facts.

13
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:54,280
1 centimetre is 10 millimetres.

14
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:56,730
1 metre is 100 centimetres.

15
00:00:56,780 --> 00:00:59,830
1 kilometre is 1,000 metres.

16
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:05,880
For an area, the length fact is used 2 times: once for the length, and once for the width.

17
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:08,110
So you square the number.

18
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:10,730
1 centimetre is 10 millimetres.

19
00:01:10,780 --> 00:01:17,280
So 1 square centimetre is 10 times 10, which is 100 square millimetres.

20
00:01:17,330 --> 00:01:21,030
1 square metre is 10,000 square centimetres.

21
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:25,840
And 1 square kilometre is 1 million square metres.

22
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:26,560
Your turn.

23
00:01:26,610 --> 00:01:29,780
Change 2 square metres to square centimetres.

24
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:33,120
Pause the video and try it.

25
00:01:33,170 --> 00:01:37,980
Each square metre is 10,000 square centimetres.

26
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:43,090
2 times 10,000 is 20,000 square centimetres.

27
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:48,300
Going from a bigger unit to a smaller unit, you need more of them.

28
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:49,240
So multiply.

29
00:01:49,290 --> 00:01:53,500
4.5 square metres is 45,000 square centimetres.

30
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:58,060
Going from a smaller unit to a bigger unit, you need fewer.

31
00:01:58,110 --> 00:01:58,830
So divide.

32
00:01:58,880 --> 00:02:03,160
730 square millimetres is 7.3 square centimetres.

33
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:03,930
Your turn.

34
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:07,910
Change 850 square millimetres to square centimetres.

35
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:11,380
Pause the video and try it.

36
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:15,900
100 square millimetres make 1 square centimetre.

37
00:02:15,950 --> 00:02:20,680
850 divided by 100 is 8.5 square centimetres.

38
00:02:20,730 --> 00:02:22,140
Here is the method.

39
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:24,460
Step 1: write the length fact.

40
00:02:24,510 --> 00:02:28,100
For example, 1 metre is 100 centimetres.

41
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:31,450
Step 2: square it, to get the area fact.

42
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:35,690
1 square metre is 10,000 square centimetres.

43
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:38,250
Step 3: to a smaller unit, multiply.

44
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:40,580
To a bigger unit, divide.

45
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:45,110
Step 4: check that the size of your answer makes sense.

46
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:49,400
Change 0.6 square metres to square centimetres.

47
00:02:49,450 --> 00:02:53,490
Going to a smaller unit, so multiply by 10,000.

48
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:57,440
The answer is 6,000 square centimetres.

49
00:02:57,490 --> 00:03:01,200
A rug is 1.5 metres long and 40 centimetres wide.

50
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:04,130
Find its area in square metres.

51
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:07,620
Make the units the same before you multiply.

52
00:03:07,670 --> 00:03:10,460
40 centimetres is 0.4 metres.

53
00:03:10,510 --> 00:03:12,480
1.5 times 0.4 is 0.6.

54
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:15,920
The area is 0.6 square metres.

55
00:03:15,970 --> 00:03:19,330
1 litre of paint covers 10 square metres.

56
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:23,570
A wall measures 500 centimetres by 280 centimetres.

57
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,200
How much paint is needed?

58
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:30,870
Change the lengths to metres first: 5 metres by 2.8 metres.

59
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:33,720
The area is 14 square metres.

60
00:03:33,770 --> 00:03:36,050
14 divided by 10 is 1.4.

61
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:39,410
You need 1.4 litres of paint.

62
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:42,660
Change 3 square metres to square centimetres.

63
00:03:42,710 --> 00:03:44,330
Here is Pita's working.

64
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:46,910
Which line goes wrong first?

65
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,240
Line 2 is wrong.

66
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:50,490
100 is the fact for length.

67
00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:57,220
For area, you must square it: 1 square metre is 10,000 square centimetres.

68
00:03:57,270 --> 00:04:02,990
3 times 10,000 is 30,000 square centimetres.

69
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:05,110
Paper sizes are built on area.

70
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:10,460
The largest sheet, called A0, has an area of exactly 1 square metre.

71
00:04:10,510 --> 00:04:17,030
Fold it in half 4 times, and you get 16 sheets of A4, the paper in your printer.

72
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:21,070
So 1 sheet of A4 is 10,000 divided by 16.

73
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:25,260
That is about 625 square centimetres.

74
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:26,620
One last question.

75
00:04:26,670 --> 00:04:29,860
A tile is 50 centimetres by 50 centimetres.

76
00:04:29,910 --> 00:04:32,430
What is its area in square metres?

77
00:04:32,480 --> 00:04:36,240
Pause the video and work it out.

78
00:04:36,290 --> 00:04:38,380
Change to metres first.

79
00:04:38,430 --> 00:04:41,080
50 centimetres is 0.5 metres.

80
00:04:41,130 --> 00:04:44,990
0.5 times 0.5 is 0.25 square metres.

81
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:50,200
To remember: 1 square centimetre is 100 square millimetres.

82
00:04:50,250 --> 00:04:54,650
1 square metre is 10,000 square centimetres.

83
00:04:54,700 --> 00:04:58,210
Square the length fact to get the area fact.

84
00:04:58,260 --> 00:05:00,120
To a smaller unit, multiply.

85
00:05:00,170 --> 00:05:02,380
To a bigger unit, divide.

86
00:05:02,430 --> 00:05:06,540
Make the units the same before you multiply lengths.

87
00:05:06,590 --> 00:05:11,950
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.1 on Camday.
